peak for a lot of litanites that we  have very little faith in the findings  of the transportation safety board and  we are incredibly disappointed  global news  prince william has taken a shot at rich  entrepreneurs competing to send tourists  to space he says they should focus  instead on ways to repair and protect  the planet  we need  some of the world's greatest brains and  minds fixed on trying to repair this  planet not trying to find the next place  to go and live  it was a swipe by the future king at  billionaires jeff bezos elon musk and  richard branson who are all vying to  usher in a new era of private commercial  space travel the interview also airs a  day after william shatner's trip to the  stars prince william's first earth shot  winners will be announced on sunday five  projects offering innovative inspiring  solutions to climate change will get 1.6  million dollars to pursue their plans  still ahead the deadly protest sparked  by the investigation into beirut's port  explosion  in southern taiwan at least 46 people  are dead and dozens more injured after a  fire at a high-rise building it happened  early this morning there are reports it  was home to many poor elderly and  disabled people an investigation into  the cause is underway  and in beirut gunfire broke out in the  lebanese capital where there's intense  anger about the investigation into last  year's huge explosion at the city's port  at least six people were killed dozens  more injured it is the most violent  street fighting in beirut in years some  people fled their homes and school  children ducked for cover as armed  fighters exchanged fire for hours with  automatic rifles and rocket-propelled  grenades the lebanese army eventually  arrested at least nine people anger has  been building since the iran-backed  hezbollah militia and its shiite allies  demanded the removal of the judge  investigating the port explosion saying  the whole thing has become politicized  the victims families support the judge's  work  nobody has been held responsible for the  august 2020 blast that killed 219 people  a fire ignited more than 2 700 tons of  ammonium nitrate that had been  improperly stored for years  lebanon's month-old government has been  facing pressure to get to the bottom of  the blast and deal with lebanon's  worsening economic crisis  a danish man is in custody after a night  of terror in a norwegian town a man shot  people with a bow and arrow a crime  norwegian police say was terrorism five  people are dead including four women  many of the victims were targeted in a  supermarket in a small town near  norway's capital oslo a 37-year-old man  is in custody police say the suspect had  converted to islam and was previously  flagged as having been radicalized they  believe he acted alone police say the  suspect is cooperating but there's no  word on a motive  bend it like davies next could this  soccer star be canada's ticket to the  world cup  alfonso davies keeps it obsessed  davies are you kidding me  it's no secret he is one of the best but  that goal by canada's alfonso davies in  last night's world cup qualifier against  panama was so astonishing even the  announcer could hardly believe it from  the way he raced to the ball stole it  from under the feet of a defender and  then buried it in the net there is a  reason it's being called one of the  greatest moments ever in canadian men's  soccer there are more world cup  qualifier games to come and as eric  sorenson reports the canadian men's team  is ready  canada's greatest it starts with alfonso  davies pure unmatched speed from where  he is on the pitch davies races past  everyone to keep the ball inbound david  plays it down the line look out that  ball steak in and davies is on it davies  takes it away  and then it's davey's pure soccer  instincts a tour de force of soccer  skill the likes of which canadian men's  soccer has never seen before  an  individual piece of brilliance coming in  game we knew how to win this game you  know to keep our walk-up hopes alive and  which we did davey's personal story is  even more awe-inspiring born in this  refugee camp in ghana his family came to  edmonton when he was five he began  playing soccer and dreaming my goal is a  play to reach a professional level  he reached the professional level at age  15 with the vancouver whitecaps then on  to one of the world's elite teams  germany's bayern munich where he has won  championships  it's just it's remarkable to watch and  it's fun as a fan because we've honestly  never seen it for decades canada has  seen only futility on the international  stage  honduras wins the match 2-1 four years  ago canada once again could not even  make this region's six team qualifying  playoffs this year canada is not only in  the tournament but has just jumped ahead  of panama into third place and it's the  top three teams that will qualify for  next year's world cup that's something  canada hasn't done since 1986 and now is  one step closer what you've seen tonight  is everything combined the heart the  spirit the talent  it's a proud night for our for our  country the inspiration of christine  sinclair and women's soccer and  development of the men's game with  talent like jonathan david and taejang  buchanan is causing support to mushroom  for canadian fans and players who dream  like alfonso davies did i think you're  seeing now  more people getting an opportunity to  play this game and having the ability to  see themselves in the bright lights  lights that are shining brightly on this  player and this team not yet a soccer  power but getting there  eric sorensen global news toronto  and that is global national for this  thursday i'm donna friesen tonight's  your canada is this former sask wheat  pool elevator in flaxcomb saskatchewan  there are beautiful spots all over  canada please email yours to viewers at  globalnational.com  thanks for watching take care of  yourselves bye bye